{"type":"assistant","uuid":"c9201668-bd9c-4001-9962-7a7b979bd6b9","session_id":"ecb49144-2540-4c5b-ae85-6b6c9450ad71","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"c9201668-bd9c-4001-9962-7a7b979bd6b9","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me now look at the specific `onSwiped` implementations more carefully, and also look at the layout files for the queue fragment and the empty view handling. The key insight from the bug report is:\n\n1. \"Undo snackar action should work\" - note the typo \"snackar\" which matches the search results\n2. \"Undo action does not work when the item is the only one in the list\"\n3. \"Empty view is removed and list is displayed\"\n4. \"List contains an item (layout inspector), but it seems to be moved outside of the screen\"\n\nThis is interesting - when you swipe out the last item and try to undo, the list seems to move the item outside the screen. This suggests the issue is with the RecyclerView layout - specifically that when the item is added back via undo, the RecyclerView's layout might be stale.\n \nThe sequence here is: user swipes away the final item triggering the database deletion, then presses Undo which re-adds it to the database, but the RecyclerView isn't properly refreshing - it's showing the empty view or the new item appears off-screen. I need to examine the onFragmentLoaded method in QueueFragment to understand how the UI updates after the undo operation completes. Looking at the event handling, I notice the issue: `notifyItemRemoved(position)` only notifies the adapter that an item was removed, but doesn't trigger a full layout pass. When the list reaches zero items, the RecyclerView stays in a stale state with the item view off-screen. Then when Undo re-adds the item via `addQueueItemAt`, the EventBus posts another `QueueEvent.REMOVED` which calls `notifyItemInserted(position)`, but the RecyclerView might not properly re-layout because it's still recovering from the removal animation. The real problem is likely in the order of operations—when the user swipes an item away, `notifyItemRemoved(position)` is called immediately, but then the Snackbar is shown and the item is removed from the database. If the user undos before the snackbar duration expires, `addQueueItemAt` is called which re-adds the item to the database and posts back through EventBus, but by then the RecyclerView might be in a bad state showing the empty view instead of the re-added item. the database, the ItemTouchHelper callback doesn't update the adapter at all—the Fragment's EventBus handler handles the UI update separately. When the undo happens, `addQueueItemAt` is called with the item and position, which triggers an EventBus event that posts back to the Fragment's `onEventMainThread` method, where the adapter gets notified that a new item was inserted at that position.\n\nThe bug report mentions the item appears to be \"moved outside of the screen,\" which suggests the RecyclerView's layout state might not be recalculating correctly after an empty list gets a new item. I need to trace through `DBWriter.addQueueItemAt` to see how it updates the queue in the database and whether it's properly triggering the adapter notification.\n\nLooking at the event flow more carefully, I'm seeing a potential mismatch: `DBWriter.removeQueueItem` posts a `QueueEvent.REMOVED` event that calls `notifyItemRemoved(position)`, but when undoing, `DBWriter.addQueueItemAt` calls `addQueueItem` instead, which might be posting a different event type or the wrong event altogether. This could explain why the item disappears or gets positioned incorrectly after an undo operation. Looking at the `markItemPlayed` call in the swipe handler—it marks items as played regardless of their current state. The `ItemTouchHelper.onSwiped` method itself doesn't notify the adapter, which could be problematic if the animation is already triggered when the EventBus event arrives to actually remove the item from the data source. I should also examine how `DBWriter.addQueueItem` handles notifications when adding the item back.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
