{"type":"assistant","uuid":"d15cf89f-79dd-40a3-b8cb-c8e48a3c8d93","session_id":"ecb49144-2540-4c5b-ae85-6b6c9450ad71","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"d15cf89f-79dd-40a3-b8cb-c8e48a3c8d93","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe exploration agent confirmed my diagnosis. All modifications are applied and verified. Here's a final summary:\n\n## Diagnosis Confirmed\n\nThe bug occurs because `notifyItemInserted()` fails to properly render the item when the RecyclerView transitions from 0 items → 1 item. The adapter's item count goes to 0 (empty view shown), then back to 1, but `notifyItemInserted()` doesn't trigger a full layout pass — the item's view gets created but positioned outside the visible area.\n\n## Fix Applied (3 files, 3 screens)\n\n**Patch:** `fix-undo-last-item.patch`\n\n### 1. `QueueFragment.java` — Queue screen\n| Change | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ADDED` event | `notifyItemInserted(position)` | `notifyDataSetChanged()` + `smoothScrollToPosition(0)` |\n| `ADDED` event | No bounds check | Validates position range and item nullability |\n| `REMOVED` event | No bounds check | Checks `position >= 0` before removing |\n\n### 2. `FavoriteEpisodesFragment.java` — Episodes→Favorites screen\n- Undo now calls `listAdapter.notifyDataSetChanged()` + `recyclerView.smoothScrollToPosition(0)` after re-adding the item\n\n### 3. `AllEpisodesFragment.java` — affects Episodes→New (via `markItemAsSeenWithUndo`)\n- Undo now calls `listAdapter.notifyDataSetChanged()` + `recyclerView.smoothScrollToPosition(0)` after marking the item as new\n\n**Build note:** The project cannot be built in this environment (jcenter.bintray.com is offline, and network access is blocked), so the fix is verified through code review rather than compilation/testing."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":80860,"output_tokens":423,"cache_read_input_tokens":12576,"total_tokens":81283}}}
